{
  "slug": "next-task",
  "name": "Next Task",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Autonomous workflow orchestrator that takes a task from discovery to production through 12 coordinated phases — exploration, planning, implementation, multi-agent review, and shipping. Pick a task from GitHub/GitLab/local sources, approve a plan, and the rest runs autonomously: git worktree creation, code generation, deslop, agnix, audit-project review loop, sync-docs, gate-and-ship. Two-file state management lets you `--resume` from any phase across session boundaries. 8 specialist agents with model selection (opus for exploration/planning, sonnet for review/CI, haiku for mechanical execution) keep token costs predictable. Workflow enforcement gates prevent skipping reviews or tests.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **8 agents**, **2 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `discover-tasks` (Use when user asks to \\\"discover tasks\\\", \\\"find next task\\\", \\\"prioritize issues\\\", \\\"what should I work on\\\", or…)\n- **Agents** (8): `ci-fixer` (Fix CI failures and PR comments), `ci-monitor` (Monitor CI status and PR comments with sleep/check loops), `exploration-agent` (Deep codebase analysis for understanding task context), `implementation-agent` (Execute approved implementation plans with high-quality code), `planning-agent` (Design detailed implementation plans for tasks), `simple-fixer` (Execute simple, pre-defined code fixes), `task-discoverer` (Use when user asks to 'discover tasks', 'find next task', 'what should I work on', or 'list open…), `worktree-manager` (Create and manage git worktrees for isolated task development)\n- **Commands** (2): `delivery-approval` (Validate task completion and approve for shipping), `next-task` (Master workflow orchestrator with autonomous task-to-production automation)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SubagentStop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install next-task@claude-community` from `agent-sh/next-task`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 8,
    "hook": 1,
